          "changeMeaning": "A single translucent domain appears to concretize the idea that each electron pair region counts as one domain. This primes students to build up the steric number before naming geometries.",
          "narration": "Each bond counts as one domain, and each lone pair counts as one domain too. For water, you have two bonding pairs and two lone pairs: four electron domains total."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "s1_clip2",
          "audioClip": "vsepr_scene1_lewis_to_3d",
