                  "text": "Steps:\n1) Count electron domains\n2) Determine steric number\n3) Choose electron-domain geometry\n4) Convert to molecular geometry (ignore lone pairs in shape)",
                  "fontSize": 30
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "The workflow panel updates to a clear step-by-step algorithm, preparing students for the next scene where domains physically rearrange into canonical geometries.",
          "narration": "Now convert that count into a 3D prediction. VSEPR gives you the electron-domain geometry first, then you convert to molecular geometry by noting which domains are lone pairs."
        }
